`STATUS=OK rows=12 findings=0 unknown=0`, `GPC` prints `PASS`, `RCC` prints its `OK:` line, `G diff --numstat HEAD -- AGENTS.md` prints `1`, `1` and `AGENTS.md`, `sed -n 65p AGENTS.md | wc -c` prints 205, `sed -n 35p $CUR | rg -c -- '--json - --format json'` prints 1 and `comm -23 <(G show HEAD:$AMM | jq -r '.derived.history[].sha256' | sort) <(jq -r '.derived.history[].sha256' $AMM | sort)` prints nothing.\n104: \n105: ### Wave 3\n106: - [ ] T016 [C] Regenerate every runtime copy of the commands and the agents (`.claude/commands`, `.cursor/commands`, `.codex/prompts`, `.pi/prompts`, `.dsh/prompts`, `.codex/agents`, `.pi/agents`, `.dsh/agents`). Run `node $MS`, then the three `sync-prompts` and the three `sync-agents` generators of `PSY` and `ASY` without `--check`. Verify: `SRM` prints `[runtime-mirror-sync] visibility claude 44/44, cursor 44/44` and `PASS: 256 mirrors across 10 trees are in sync.`, `PSY` prints `45` three times, `ASY` prints `11` three times, `AMSC` is in sync, `readlink .claude/commands/create/sk-skill.md` prints `../../../.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md`, `readlink .cursor/commands/create-sk-skill.md` prints `../../.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md`, `ls .codex/prompts/create-sk-skill.md .pi/prompts/create-sk-skill.md .dsh/prompts/create-sk-skill.md` lists three files, `find .claude/commands .cursor/commands .codex/prompts .pi/prompts .dsh/prompts \\( -iname skill.md -o -name create-skill.md \\)` prints nothing and `readlink .claude/skills` prints `../.skilled/skills`.\n107: - [ ] T017 [C] Rebuild the advisor, restart the worktree's daemon and re-embed (`$ADV/dist`, the advisor database). Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, restart the advisor daemon this worktree serves, then `CLI skill_graph_scan --trusted --format text`. Verify: the build exits 0, `TC` exits 0, `rg -c 'appear' $ADV/dist/runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.js` prints at least 1, `rg -c 'create:sk-skill' $ADV/dist/runtime/lib/command-attach.js` prints at least 1 and the scan prints its status with no error. When Ollama does not answer, mark this task `[B]` and start nothing.\n108: - [ ] T018 [C] Read the fixture floors and take the real capture before lane D (`$SP/real-before-d.json`). Run `FLOOR` without `--write`, then `REAL` into `$SP/real-before-d.json` and read it. Verify: `FLOOR` prints typed recall of 24 of 44 or more, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, typed delivery `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}` or a `combined` of 44, a plain tune `combined` of 23 or more and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`. The `REAL` read prints typed 24 of 44 or more, false offers `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` in both columns and `[false,false,false]`, and its tune and holdout counts are written into `$SP/before.txt` as the lane D before line, holdout as a count only.\n109: \n110: ### Wave 4\n111: - [ ] T019 [P] Lane D. Add intent phrases to the five scored commands that have no recommendation (`RTS`, `SSK` and the `DER` outputs). Take the phrases in `added` for `/doctor:install`, `/doctor:setup`, `/doctor:speckit`, `/doctor:update` and `/speckit:search` from `LIN`, and leave `/create:skill-parent` out. Before adding them, read the prompts of `cmd-doctor-install-plain-tune-01`, `cmd-doctor-setup-plain-tune-01`, `cmd-doctor-speckit-plain-tune-01`, `cmd-doctor-update-plain-tune-01` and `cmd-speckit-search-plain-tune-01` from `CORPUS` by id, each after checking that its `split` is `tune`. Compare each phrase with its command's tune prompt after lowercasing and collapsing spaces, and rewrite any phrase that equals that prompt or holds it whole as a paraphrase that keeps the intent words and changes the rest, because a phrase copied from a tune prompt counts as gain only on tune. Never read or compare a holdout row. Add the four doctor commands' phrases to `trigger_phrases` of their routes in `RTS` and the search phrases to `userIntent.ownedSignals` of `/speckit:search` in `SSK`, then run `DER`. Verify: a script that compares every added phrase with the five tune prompts on the same normalized text prints `0`, `RV` holds `32 routes validated`, `DPR` prints `STATUS=OK` with `phrases=` higher than `$SP/before.txt` by the number of doctor phrases added, `DRV` prints `\"changed\": []`, `jq empty $SSK` passes and `TC` exits 0.\n112: \n113: ### Wave 5\n114: - [ ] T020 [C] Rebuild, restart, re-embed and take the real capture after lane D (`$ADV/dist`, the advisor database, `$SP/real-after-d.json`). Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, restart the daemon, run `CLI skill_graph_scan --trusted --format text`, then `REAL` into `$SP/real-after-d.json` and read it. Verify: the build exits 0, the scan prints no error, typed reads 24 of 44 or more, false offers read `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` in both columns, the floor rows print `[false,false,false]` and the holdout count is at least 2 above the lane D before line from T018. Record the tune counts as built in, not as gain. A smaller holdout gain is reported as measured, and no phrase changes after this count is read.\n115: \n116: ### Wave 6\n117: - [ ] T021 [P] Recapture the fixture baseline and check the scorer eval (`BASE`, and `$RA/scorer-eval-baseline.json` only when its values move). Run `node $CAP --write`, `FLOOR` and `EVAL`. When `EVAL` differs from the committed baseline and still holds the floor, recapture it with `node $RA/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs --write` as its header documents and run `V tests/parity/scorer-eval-baseline-ratchet.vitest.ts tests/parity/scorer-eval-baseline-capture-date.vitest.ts`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints typed recall of 24 of 44 or more, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, a typed delivery `combined` of 44 of 44, a plain tune `combined` of 23 or more and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `jq -c '.rows[\"cmd-doctor-mcp-plain-tune-01\"].offered, .rows[\"cmd-doctor-skill-advisor-plain-tune-01\"].offered' $BASE` prints `true` and `false`, `jq -r '.commands | keys[]' $BASE | rg -cx '/create:sk-skill'` prints 1, `OLD $BASE` prints nothing, `SLICE` reports 0 failed and `EVAL` prints at least `[160,50,21,5]` with the fourth value no higher than 5.\n118: \n119: ### Wave 7\n120: - [ ] T022 [C] Observe Claude's command folder without a model session (`$SP/claude-observed.txt`). Run `SRM`, `ls .claude/commands/create` and `find .claude/commands -iname skill.md | wc -l`. Verify: `SRM` prints `visibility claude 44/44`, the listing holds 13 entries with `sk-skill.md` among them and the count prints 0. These three facts are the proof a coordinator can take. Claude's own listing is T023's.\n121: - [ ] T023 [C] Ask the operator for one live Claude Code listing of the regenerated tree (`$SP/claude-listing.txt`). It needs a model session, so it is the operator's to run and confirm. Write the expected names with `(cd .claude/commands && find . -name '*.md' -not -name 'local-*' | sed -e 's|^\\./||' -e 's|\\.md$||' -e 's|/|:|') | sort > $SP/claude-expected.txt`. In a directory from `mktemp -d` outside any repository, copy the tree with `cp -RL .claude/commands <tmp>/x/.claude/commands`, start Claude Code once in `<tmp>/x` with the prompt \"List the names of every entry your Skill tool offers, one per line, and nothing else.\", save the answer to `$SP/claude-listing.txt` and delete the temp directory. Verify: `wc -l < $SP/claude-expected.txt` prints 44 and `comm -23 $SP/claude-expected.txt <(sed -E 's/^[-*/ ]+//' $SP/claude-listing.txt | sort -u)` prints nothing, so `create:sk-skill` and the twelve other `create:*` names are listed. Until the operator runs it, this task stays open and REQ-012 rests on T022.\n122: - [ ] T024 [C] Read the live doctor brief and the CLI answer for the two doctor rows (`$SP/doctor-live.txt`). For each of `cmd-doctor-mcp-plain-tune-01` and `cmd-doctor-skill-advisor-plain-tune-01`, build the hook payload with `jq -c --arg cwd \"$PWD\" 'select(.id == \"<id>\") | if .split == \"tune\" then {prompt, cwd: $cwd, hook_event_name: \"UserPromptSubmit\", session_id: \"doctor-helper-check\"} else error(\"not a tune row\") end' $CORPUS`, pipe it into `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD node $HOOK` and keep `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`. Then build `{prompt}` the same way, pipe it into `CLI advisor_recommend --json - --format json` and keep `jq -c '.data.recommendations[] | select(.skillId == \"command-doctor-helper\") | [.command, .policy]'`. Write each result beside its row id, never the prompt. Verify: the mcp brief holds a line starting `Also: /doctor:helper`, the mcp CLI line prints `[\"/doctor:helper\",\"run\"]`, the skill-advisor brief holds no `/doctor:` and its CLI line prints nothing.\n123: - [ ] T025 [C] Run the brief-cost script once and prove the health log is untouched (`$SP/brief-cost-run.txt`). Record `find \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/speckit-skill-advisor-metrics\" -type f -exec wc -l {} +`, run `node $MBC --rows cmd-create-agent-typed-01` and record its exit code and its first line, then record the same `find` again. Verify: the two `find` outputs are identical, and the script either exits 0 with one live row or exits 2 with `degraded_brief`. Record which, and change no code on either answer.\n124: \n125: ### Wave 8\n126: - [ ] T026 Write the changelog entry for the breaking rename at `v2.10.0.0`, the version the operator chose in Q3 (the `sk-doc` changelog entry and the `version` fields of `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md`, `hub-router.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `description.json`). Write the entry through the `sk-create-changelog` workflow as `v2.10.0.0`, a minor bump whose text calls out the break, and set the four version fields to `2.10.0.0`. Its first line of substance says `/create:skill` is now `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime with no alias, and why. Edit no existing entry. Verify: `G status --short -- '*/changelog/*'` lists only the new entry, `G diff --quiet HEAD -- .skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog .skilled/changelog` exits 0 and `PSC` holds `all hard invariants passed, 0 warnings`.\n127: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n128: \n129: ---\n130: \n131: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n132: ## Phase 3: Verification\n133: \n134: - [ ] T027 [C] Run every floor and check (`$SP/after.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `VALL`, `DALL`, `DRV`, `SRM`, `NMST`, `PSY`, `ASY`, `AMSC`, `AMC`, `MAN`, `GPC`, `RCC`, `CRS`, `PSC`, `CCM`, `RV` and `DPR`, and write each output beside its line in `$SP/before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` holds every floor in REQ-007, `EVAL` prints at least `[160,50,21,5]` with the fourth value no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed, `DALL` reports `fail 0`, `DRV` prints `\"changed\": []`, `SRM` prints `visibility claude 44/44, cursor 44/44`, `NMST` reports `fail 0`, `PSY`, `ASY` and `AMSC` pass, `AMC`, `MAN`, `GPC` and `RCC` pass, `CRS` prints both lines, `PSC` holds `all hard invariants passed`, `CCM` prints `STATUS=OK`, `RV` holds `32 routes validated` and `DPR` starts `STATUS=OK`.\n135: - [ ] T028 [C] Check the rename's end state and the boundaries. Verify: `OLD` prints exactly the nine `KEPT` files, `rg -l -F 'create:sk-skill' .skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md .skilled/skills/sk-doc/mode-registry.json $ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` lists all three, `G diff --quiet HEAD -- .claude/skills .skilled/commands/create/skill-parent.md $ADV/lib/render.ts` exits 0, every `KEPT` file is unchanged by `G diff --quiet HEAD --`, `G diff --stat HEAD -- '*package.json' '*package-lock.json'` prints nothing, `G diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled .claude .cursor .codex .pi .dsh AGENTS.md | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|[Pp]hase [0-9]|[Rr]ank [0-9]|R4-P2)\"` prints nothing, `G diff --numstat HEAD -- AGENTS.md` prints `1`, `1` and `AGENTS.md`, and `G status --short -- .skilled .claude .cursor .codex .pi .dsh AGENTS.md README.md CONTRIBUTING.md` lists only files named in this phase's tasks.\n136: - [ ] T029 [C] Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence (`implementation-summary.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n137: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n138: \n139: ---\n140: \n141: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n142: ## Completion Criteria\n143: \n144: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`, with T023 allowed open only while it waits on the operator\n145: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n146: - [ ] `OLD` lists only the nine `KEPT` files, `SRM` prints `visibility claude 44/44`, `BASE` holds every floor, the real holdout count rose by at least 2 in T020 and every floor holds against `$SP/before.txt`\n147: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n148: \n149: ---\n150: \n151: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n152: ## Cross-References\n153: \n154: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n155: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n156: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n157: - **Research**: `../009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-3.md` and `../009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-4.md`\n158: - **Review**: `../review/review-report.md`\n159: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n160: \n161: ---\n162: \n163: ## Verification Checklist\n164: \n165: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n166: ## Verification Protocol\n167: \n168: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n169: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n170: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n171: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n172: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n173: \n174: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A moved floor blocks the phase.\n175: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n176: \n177: ---\n178: \n179: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n180: ## Pre-Implementation\n181: \n182: - [ ] CHK-001 [P0] The base is clean and phase 015 is committed (T001). Evidence: the T001 verify lines.\n183: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] The before numbers are in `scratch/before.txt` and match `spec.md` section 2 (T002). Evidence: the T002 verify lines.\n184: - [ ] CHK-003 [P0] The command file moved with its history (T003). Evidence: the `R` status line.\n185: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n186: \n187: ---\n188: \n189: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n190: ## Code Quality\n191: \n192: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `TC` exits 0 and `node --check` passes on `MS`, `MBC` and the schema helper. Evidence: `$SP/after.txt` and the T004, T007 and T013 verifies.\n193: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No added code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a task id, a rank id or a finding id (T028). Evidence: the T028 label scan prints nothing.\n194: - [ ] CHK-012 [P0] Every generated file was written by its generator, and every generator check passes (T014, T015, T016, T019, T021). Evidence: `DRV`, `SRM`, `PSY`, `ASY`, `MAN`, `GPC` and `SLICE`.\n195: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] `AGENTS.md` changes on line 65 only (T015, T028). Evidence: the `numstat` line reads `1`, `1`.\n196: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n197: \n198: ---\n199: \n200: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n201: ## Testing Checklist\n202: \n203: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] Every floor holds (T021, T027). Evidence: `$SP/after.txt` beside `$SP/before.txt`.\n204: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The old-name scan lists only the nine kept files (T028). Evidence: the `OLD` output.\n205: - [ ] CHK-022 [P0] The mirror check reads 44 of 44 with no allowlist and fails on a capitalised `SKILL.md` (T004, T016). Evidence: `NMST` and the `SRM` line.\n206: - [ ] CHK-023 [P0] The tests written first failed before their change and pass after it (T004, T012, T013). Evidence: `fail 2`, `fail 1` and `1 failed` before, 0 after.\n207: - [ ] CHK-024 [P1] The real holdout count rose by at least 2 with every real floor held (T018, T020). Evidence: `$SP/real-before-d.json` and `$SP/real-after-d.json`.\n208: - [ ] CHK-025 [P1] The live brief and the CLI name `/doctor:helper` on the mcp tune row and on no other doctor row checked (T024). Evidence: `$SP/doctor-live.txt`.\n209: - [ ] CHK-026 [P1] Claude's folder holds no `skill.md` in any capitalisation, and the operator's listing names all 44 (T022, T023). Evidence: `$SP/claude-observed.txt` and `$SP/claude-listing.txt`.\n210: - [ ] CHK-027 [P1] A cost run leaves the shared health log unchanged (T025). Evidence: `$SP/brief-cost-run.txt`.\n211: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n212: \n213: ---\n214: \n215: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n216: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n217: \n218: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each item has a class: the rename `cross-consumer` (55 files and five runtimes), the collapse check `class-of-bug` (any folder, any capitalisation), the doctor cue `instance-only`, the Gate 2 line `cross-consumer` (three copies), the intent phrases `matrix/evidence` (fixture and real captures) and the cost run `instance-only`. Evidence: the classes match the affected surfaces in `plan.md`.\n219: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producers: the `OLD` scan covers every spelling of the old name across hidden runtime trees, and `rg -n \"skill\\.md\" $MS` lists only the case-free comparisons. Evidence: the two outputs.\n220: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Every consumer of a changed output is in the `plan.md` addendum. Evidence: the generator list and the `OLD` scan name no file outside it.\n221: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] The matrix axes in `plan.md` each have a case in T004, T011, T018, T020 or an existing test. Evidence: the case names and the two real captures.\n222: - [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] `VALL` runs with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset, and the T024 hook run unsets it too. Evidence: the T027 and T024 commands.\n223: - [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on. Evidence: `$SP/after.txt` and `implementation-summary.md` name it.\n224: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n225: \n226: ---\n227: \n228: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n229: ## Security\n230: \n231: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No task prints holdout prompt text or opens `holdout-prompts.jsonl`. Evidence: the holdout corpus row changed by a count-only `sed` in T010, every capture publishes holdout as counts, and T011, T019 and T024 read tune rows by id after checking the split.\n232: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] No worker starts a model session, a daemon or Ollama, moves a file with git or writes under the home folder. Evidence: T003, T016, T017, T018, T020 and T022 to T025 are coordinator tasks, and T023 is the operator's.\n233: - [ ] CHK-032 [P1] The documented direct call sends the prompt on stdin (T015). Evidence: `sed -n 65p AGENTS.md` and the T012 case.\n234: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n235: \n236: ---\n237: \n238: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n239: ## Documentation\n240: \n241: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same numbers. Evidence: 55 files to nine, 32 of 44 to 44 of 44, `offered` false to true, a 188-byte line to a 204-byte line and the holdout delta read the same in each.\n242: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The mirror README, the hook guide, the root docs and the changelog entry match the code (T004, T008, T009, T026). Evidence: their verify commands print what they say.\n243: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n244: \n245: ---\n246: \n247: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n248: ## File Organization\n249: \n250: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Every measurement lives in `scratch/` and no probe script is left in the tree. Evidence: `ls scratch` lists the files the tasks name.\n251: - [ ] CHK-051 [P1] No file outside the tasks' list changed (T028). Evidence: the T028 status line.\n252: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n253: \n254: ---\n255: \n256: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n257: ## Verification Summary\n258: \n259: | Category | Total | Verified |\n260: |----------|-------|----------|\n261: | P0 Items | 15 | 0/15 |\n262: | P1 Items | 13 | 0/13 |\n263: | P2 Items | 0 | 0/0 |\n264: \n265: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-13\n266: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-