{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582839561,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d0ffeK3FWMmeG07e8v3","part":{"partID":"prt_1d578fadd001qZ7h2kWGuJjMAX","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d0ffeK3FWMmeG07e8v3","messageID":"msg_1d578eb5a001U2OAtsCIwwww4h","type":"tool","id":"call_e12a86f0c69f4d999088c3db","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md","oldString":"| Claude Code | Yes, through the Skill tool, as a shortcut for the names it lists: 33 of the 45 names, including one `create` entry and none of the other twelve `create:*` names | The Skill tool lists names, not files. `create/skill.md` collides with the `SKILL.md` convention on a case-insensitive disk, so the folder reads as one skill |","newString":"| Claude Code | Yes, through the Skill tool, as a shortcut for the names it lists | The Skill tool lists names, not files. A command file named `skill.md` in any capitalisation makes Claude Code read its folder as one skill, an open upstream bug, so no command file carries that name |"},"output":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md","patch":"Index: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\n===================================================================\n--- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\n+++ .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\n@@ -100,9 +100,9 @@\n The document behind a surfaced command is `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md`. The model reads that document in full and follows it, on every runtime. It never tells the user to type a slash command, and it asks the user to type one only when it cannot read the file.\n \n | Runtime | Model can start a command itself | Basis |\n |---|---|---|\n-| Claude Code | Yes, through the Skill tool, as a shortcut for the names it lists: 33 of the 45 names, including one `create` entry and none of the other twelve `create:*` names | The Skill tool lists names, not files. `create/skill.md` collides with the `SKILL.md` convention on a case-insensitive disk, so the folder reads as one skill |\n+| Claude Code | Yes, through the Skill tool, as a shortcut for the names it lists | The Skill tool lists names, not files. A command file named `skill.md` in any capitalisation makes Claude Code read its folder as one skill, an open upstream bug, so no command file carries that name |\n | Codex | No | The mirror is a pointer stub that tells the model to read the command file. There is no `.codex/skills` |\n | Cursor | No model path found, and the brief is dormant | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Cursor docs were not fetched |\n | Devin | No command surface at all | Skills are exposed, commands are not |\n | Pi | No model path found | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Pi docs were not fetched, so this is unverified beyond the repository |\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\",\"oldString\":\"| Claude Code | Yes, through the Skill tool, as a shortcut for the names it lists: 33 of the 45 names, including one `create` entry and none of the other twelve `create:*` names | The Skill tool lists names, not files. `create/skill.md` collides with the `SKILL.md` convention on a case-insensitive disk, so the folder reads as one skill |\",\"newString\":\"| Claude Code | Yes, through the Skill tool, as a shortcut for the names it lists | The Skill tool lists names, not files. A command file named `skill.md` in any capitalisation makes Claude Code read its folder as one skill, an open upstream bug, so no command file carries that name |\"}"},"time":{"start":1794582837981,"end":1794582839561}}}}
